[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Expressive Launcher 3.1.5 QA — Swipe Right, Search Bright[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Official Release Announcement & Download Links[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

Welcome to Expressive Launcher 3.1.5 (Build 47)! This build fixes Google Discover and brings two Android 17 QPR2 touches to Home: Google's own search bar in the dock and Pixel's new long-press menu.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's New & Improved[/B][/SIZE]

1. [B]Google Discover works again[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]What went wrong:[/B] if Expressive didn't have install permission yet, setup offered the standalone [I]Expressive Feed Companion[/I] download. That APK was signed for the retired Google Play edition and refuses to connect to Expressive from GitHub. Discover stayed blank while settings said it was on, and Android wouldn't let the built-in helper replace it.
[*][B]Set up Google Discover[/B] is now always shown. It installs the Discover helper included with Expressive. When Android asks, choose [B]Always allow[/B] for Expressive under [I]Install unknown apps[/I]; [I]Ask every time[/I] isn't enough. If Play Protect shows [B]App scan recommended[/B], tap [B]Scan app[/B], then [B]Install[/B].
[*][B]Installed the old companion?[/B] Settings now offer [B]Replace Discover support[/B]. It opens Android's uninstall confirmation, then installs the built-in helper.
[*]Discover support is now FOSS-only. The standalone companion is retired, its download page explains the built-in setup, and the helper only trusts the launcher it shipped with.

[/LIST]
2. [B]Google's own search bar, when you want it[/B]
[LIST]
[*]New free [B]Home screen > Google search bar[/B] switch puts the Google app's own search widget in the dock, like Pixel Launcher on Android 17 QPR2, with search, voice and Lens. The buttons come from the Google app, so AI Mode appears when Google offers it for your account.
[*]Android asks once, when you turn the switch on, whether Expressive may create the widget. Tap [B]Create[/B]. Tap [B]Cancel[/B] and nothing changes. Expressive never shows that prompt on its own.
[*]Fixed an empty bar: the Google search bar option picked a Google widget that draws nothing in the dock.

[/LIST]
3. [B]Android 17 QPR2 home menu[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Long-press Home for one wallpaper-tinted card instead of separate tiles, with filled icons and a gear for [B]Home settings[/B].
[*]The top row shows your current wallpaper, followed by up to three recent ones. Tap the current one to open [B]Wallpaper & style[/B].
[*]The menu keeps the same card if you turn the wallpaper row off.

[/LIST]
For developers: debug and release builds can be installed side by side again.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💎 Expressive Pro & Free Core[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Free Core[/B]: always supported, ad-free and privacy-first. Discover, the Google search bar switch and the new menu are all part of Free Core.
[*][B]Expressive Pro ($4.99 one-time)[/B]: unlocks deep personalization such as grid sizing, typography, gestures, per-app icon overrides and folder styles.

[/LIST]
> [I]Expressive Pro is available as a one-time $4.99 activation. Every dollar directly funds our ongoing tooling and infrastructure expenses—including automated CI/CD servers, dedicated Android 17 testing devices/emulators, signing pipelines, and active continuous development—keeping Expressive fast, independent, and completely ad-free.[/I]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]😄 Launcher Humor[/B][/SIZE]

> [B]Q:[/B] [I]Why did Discover keep standing everyone up?[/I]
> [B]A:[/B] [I]Its ride showed up with the wrong key to the house.[/I]

> The Google search bar wanted to move into the dock right away. We told it to wait until it's invited.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

> [I]I live just left of your first page, yet I'm never in your grid. I arrive with the news whenever you reach for me. Last week I waited at the door for a friend holding the wrong key. What am I?[/I]

[SPOILER="Tap to reveal answer"]<b>Google Discover, now opened by the helper built into Expressive!</b>[/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧪 Validation[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]App unit suite: 319 tests passing, including 13 new regression tests for replacing the Discover helper, choosing and turning on Google's dock search bar, and the home menu's width and wallpaper row.
[*]Discover helper unit tests: 6 passing. CI pipeline contract tests: 279 passing.
[*]Android 17 QPR2 emulator (Google app 17.46): reproduced the blank Discover with the retired companion; verified the built-in setup and [B]Replace Discover support[/B], including Play Protect's scan prompt; compared the dock search bar and home menu with Pixel Launcher in light and dark themes. Turned the Google search bar on and off: Android's prompt appears only then, and Cancel leaves the dock unchanged. The emulator isn't signed in to Google, so AI Mode wasn't checked there.
[*]Jenkins handles the signed QA build, emulator smoke checks and publication. No physical-device matrix is claimed for this build.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

